          {
            "commit": "3727a7c3f0f5302b073f9be4620cc0794526dbde",
            "subject": "LU-20076 tests: fewer remote commands in setupall checks"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-03 18:27:50.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "patrick bot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-11-04 06:16:47.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: do not sleep before the checks in fail()",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: do not sleep before the checks in fail()\n\nclients_up() sleeps for a second before its \"lfs df\". The\nsleep comes from fail_abort(), which once ran \"df\", allowed\nit to fail, slept and ran it again. When those calls became\nclients_up(), every caller got the sleep.\n\nfail() calls clients_up() twice: once to wake idle OSC\nconnections, then after wait_clients_import_ready() as the\nfinal check. \"lfs df\" waits for every target to answer, and\nthe second call follows a wait for the imports to be FULL,\nso neither sleep waits for anything. Call lfs_df_check()\ndirectly there. fail_abort() and the tests that call\nclients_up() keep the sleep.\n\nThat is 2 s per fail(), about 2 million failovers in 30\ndays, roughly 800 to 1000 hours of test time. With the\nchanges before this one, \"fail mds1\" went from 17 remote\ncommands to 5, 4.7 to 2.8 s on a test cluster, and 9.6 to\n3.4 s with 0.25 s added to each remote command.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=replay-single,recovery-small\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=replay-dual,insanity\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: If8e9c129bbd56b289700ab129e6dbb2721779fc1\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
